          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "submitted_at": "2026-11-13T23:45:48Z",
          "body": "## Author-side assisted review of 8dbe831a243e66aad18c601086a8e62b3c496322\n\nThis is an explicitly attributed author-side review with AI assistance. It is a COMMENT, not an independent approval or a statement that the full project is accepted.\n\nI reviewed the delivered workflow and its evidence across source verification/normalization, financial reconciliation, version and lease fencing, attributed corrections, approval/publication boundaries, restoration and local-model policy. The final evidence commit changes documentation and proof artifacts only; the executed application remains source commit `3ff93109f3ea0d9c5f4bdfd598dd35bbd4513439`.\n\n### Evidence checked\n\n- The recorded 63 runtime/contract/test/infrastructure source hashes match the executed commit. All 72 fresh baseline/local-linear semantic outputs match the earlier evaluation, excluding timing fields.\n- The original suite records 107 successful tests and no skips. The real HTTP report records 36 checks across 30 requests to a Uvicorn process with a separate model worker, including all three request/audit/job joins.\n- Baseline publishes/restores seven dossiers; raw local linear publishes/restores six. The failing seven-export assertion and original false aggregate are still present. A separate attributed subtotal correction, self-approval denial and different approver yield seven restored exports without model or parser calls.\n- Both TARs' 517 members match their recorded inventories, hashes and original bytes. All 14 ZIPs passed member/CRC checks, and all 42 exported PDFs match their original synthetic inputs. Known-secret/history checks reported no findings; this is scoped verification, not security certification.\n- Dependency auditing found zero known vulnerabilities among 32 Python runtime packages at execution time. Third-party inventory does not select or certify this project's own licence.\n\n### Findings that remain open\n\n1. Frozen local-linear footer confusion causes an extra review. Preserve the current adverse result; use a new training/tuning design and untouched holdout before claiming improvement.\n2. Bounded Qwen completes requests but fails classification/coverage quality: 3/36 correct and 0/36 eligible. Keep the profile experimental; no eligible-quality percentage can be claimed when the denominator is zero.\n3. Current-head Actions run [43529263240](https://github.com/mehdisafer/document-control-intelligence/actions/runs/43529263240) has three failed jobs with no runner and no steps. The rejection cause is not exposed. Browser rendering, container execution and Terraform schema validation therefore remain unqualified.\n4. Intended-host deployment, repository administration, the explicit project-licence choice and any public release are separate unresolved gates. No account/billing/security/visibility setting was changed.\n\nThe scoped application and local execution evidence are reviewable. Keep this PR in draft and issue #1 open until the unresolved acceptance decisions and execution prerequisites are addressed. No merge or stable-release recommendation is made by this review.\n",
          "author_login": "mehdisafer"
        },
        {
